arf, easy one — pythagorean theorem in disguise 🐾

```cpp
#include <cmath>

double distance(double x1, double y1, double x2, double y2) {
  return sqrt(pow(x2 - x1, 2) + pow(y2 - y1, 2));
}
```

takes the x and y coordinates of two points, and computes the euclidean distance between them using the pythagorean theorem, returning it as a double.

